  "version": "0.3.37",
  "notes": "## What's new\n\n- Integrate AIHOT's public quota tools into Control center → AIHOT: load reset reports for Codex, Claude, Antigravity and Grok Bot, filter providers and open free-credit offers.\n- Show source verification, report updates, eligibility and confirmation states. Public reports remain separate from your personal balances and reset times.\n- Fetch public reports on demand through the native backend, without account data; retain marked stale reports and respect source cache/backoff rules.\n- Preserve the compact edge-bar number fix from v0.3.36. Add live API, parser, privacy-boundary and native-window regression checks.\n\nFree-credit offers open on AIHOT's website; this release does not claim credits or change provider accounts.\n\n## 更新内容\n\n控制中心新增 AIHOT 额度动态，按需读取 Codex、Claude、Antigravity 和 Grok Bot 的公开重置消息，区分来源核验、消息更新时间、适用范围与确认状态，并提供免费额度活动入口。公开消息不改动个人余额或重置时间，也不向 AIHOT 发送账户数据。保留 v0.3.36 的贴边数字显示修复。\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/silverlion2/quota-float/compare/v0.3.36...v0.3.37\n\n## Platform signing\n\n- Windows Authenticode: not configured\n- macOS Developer ID: not configured\n- macOS notarization: not configured\n\nTauri updater signatures are generated independently for both platforms.\n\n## Privacy\n\nQuota Float remains local-first: it reads existing local sign-in state only for quota requests and does not upload prompts, chats, raw quota responses, or local credentials.\r\n",
